<Project>

  <!--
    Deliberately empty, and deliberately here.

    MSBuild stops at the first Directory.Build.props it finds walking up from a project, so this
    file is what stops everything under samples/ from inheriting the component's own build
    properties. That is the whole point of a PRISTINE consumer: a real consumer of these packages
    has no Directory.Build.props of ours, no vendored packaging metadata, no analyzer level we
    chose and no warning policy we set. A sample that built under the component's properties would
    be proving that our packages work inside our build, which is not the claim.

    Each sample sets what it needs for itself, in its own project file, where a reader can see it.
  -->

</Project>
